Package: tarball-manager
Version: @VERSION@-@REVISION@
Section: utils
Priority: optional
Architecture: all
Maintainer: ryovoid <rp6502293@gmail.com>
Installed-Size: @INSTALLED_SIZE@
Depends: python3 (>= 3.9),
 python3-gi (>= 3.42),
 gir1.2-gtk-4.0,
 gir1.2-adw-1,
 libglib2.0-bin,
 desktop-file-utils,
 hicolor-icon-theme,
 pkexec | policykit-1
Recommends: gtk-update-icon-cache
Homepage: https://github.com/ryovoid/tarball-manager
Description: Install Linux app tarballs as desktop applications
 Tarball Manager lets you install, manage, and update applications
 distributed as .tar.gz, .tar.xz and .tar.bz2 archives.
 .
 It detects the application's executable and icon, generates a desktop
 entry so the app shows up in the application menu, sets up a symlink on
 PATH for command-line use, and handles both per-user and system-wide
 installations.
